    "utf-8",
    "TITLE",
    "STYLE",
    "\n  html,body { margin:0; padding:0; font:16px/1.4 -apple-system, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; }\n  /* The three containers this page exists for. Each one holds an ELEMENT at\n     depth 1 and another at depth 2, which is the shape `t0-page.html` lacks:\n     there every hidden container's only descendant is a text node. */\n  #opacity-zero { opacity:0; }\n  #opacity-zero-frame { opacity:0; }\n  #frame-host   { width:300px; height:80px; border:0; }\n  #vis-hidden   { visibility:hidden; }\n  #disp-none    { display:none; }\n  /* A descendant that declares FULL opacity inside the transparent container.\n     CSS group-composites `opacity`, so this element is invisible anyway and\n     cannot re-show itself — unlike `visibility`, where the equivalent\n     declaration really does re-show. Both are measured here. */\n  #op-d2-opaque { opacity:1; }\n  #vis-d2-shown { visibility:visible; }\n  a, button     { cursor:pointer; }\n",
    "BODY",
    "\n  ",
    "MAIN",
    "id",
    "main",
    "\n    ",
    "DIV",
    "opacity-zero",
    "0",
    "\n      ",
    "P",
    "op-d1",
    "depth 1 under opacity zero\n        ",
    "BUTTON",
    "op-d2",
    "type",
    "button",
    "inline-block",
    "pointer",
    "depth 2 under opacity zero",
    "\n        ",
    "op-d2-opaque",
    "depth 2 declaring opacity one",
    "vis-hidden",
    "hidden",
    "vis-d1",
    "depth 1 under visibility hidden\n        ",
    "vis-d2",
    "depth 2 under visibility hidden",
    "vis-d2-shown",
    "depth 2 declaring visibility visible",
    "disp-none",
    "none-d1",
    "depth 1 under display none\n        ",
    "none-d2",
    "depth 2 under display none",
    "control",
    "visible control",
    "#comment",
    " OPT-IN, and it stays out of the committed capture deliberately. `?child=<url>` puts a\n         same-origin iframe inside a third `opacity:0` container, which is how the CROSS-FRAME\n         residual is measured: a child document is its own `RawFrame` with its own node array, and\n         `parent` never crosses that boundary. The committed fixture is captured WITHOUT the param\n         so it stays one document; the residual reading is a second run WITH it. ",
    "SCRIPT",
    "\n    var child = new URL(location.href).searchParams.get('child');\n    if (child) { document.getElementById('frame-host').src = child; }\n    else { document.getElementById('opacity-zero-frame').remove(); }\n  ",
    "\n\n\n"
  ]
